  data:  # b4d5
    kind: work_item  # b4d5
    title: "Independent I/O-primitive allowlist gate: every write/subprocess/network/eval/pickle/ctypes call site in packages/*/src must be on a committed allowlist (AST-based, CI)"  # b4d5
    status: todo_hard  # b4d5
    priority: 2  # b4d5
    parent:  # b4d5
    tags:  # b4d5
    - security  # b4d5
    - ci  # b4d5
    isbefore: []  # b4d5
    duplicate_of: []  # b4d5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # b4d5
    pr_ref:  # b4d5
    description: "An independent check on hypergumbo's own I/O surface that does NOT share hypergumbo's static-analysis blind spots (the self-claims are hypergumbo grading itself; every verdict carries opaque_boundary / unknown_receiver_scope caveats). A syntactic gate over packages/*/src: every call site of a risky primitive -- filesystem writes/deletes (write_text/write_bytes, open(...,'w'/'a'/'x'), shutil copy/move/rmtree, os.remove/unlink/rename/replace, Path.unlink/mkdir/touch), subprocess/os.system/exec*/spawn*, network (socket, urllib.request, http.client, httpx, requests, aiohttp, huggingface_hub/from_pretrained downloads), servers (uvicorn/HTTPServer/serve_forever), eval/exec/compile, pickle/marshal/torch.load, ctypes/cffi/dlopen, importlib/__import__ with non-literal names -- must be listed in a committed allowlist naming file, function, the CLI command(s) that reach it and why. New unlisted site -> CI fails; stale entry -> CI fails. Use AST, not grep, so catalogue strings (io_boundary/axis_meta_keys hold primitive names as DATA) don't count and aliasing (`from subprocess import run as r`) does. Initial rough grep, 2026-10-07: subprocess in 24 files (14 core, 7 tracker, 2 rust-analyzer, 1 scip-python), ~150 write/delete sites. Cross-check the allowlist against the self-claims zones (user_cache, user_out, tmp, install_artifact) and report disagreements. Owner request 2026-10-07."  # b4d5
    fields: {}  # b4d5
