- op: discuss  # c82b
  at: '2026-10-10T19:16:29Z'  # c82b
  by: agent  # c82b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c82b
  clock: 4  # c82b
  nonce: c82b  # c82b
  message: "Merged in PR #1516 (99ad3588af + 0e6e72265c ARCHITECTURE.md regen): scripts/check-io-allowlist, a stdlib-only AST gate that imports nothing from hypergumbo. It resolves import aliases and counts non-call references, and every risky-primitive site in packages/*/src must be on docs/hypergumbo.io-allowlist.yaml (264 sites / 224 entries, keyed by module+function+primitive with a count; each entry gives zone, purpose, commands and, for launches, the target program). Wired as a per-PR woodpecker step (it was green on the PR pipeline), a ci.yml job, and unconditional steps in both full-suite workflows; SECURITY.md is generated with the gate and its findings. Findings filed rather than allowlisted: INV-gujus (first sketch downloads the embedding models, contradicting runtime-cli-no-network), INV-tusos (rust-analyzer scip / scip-python launched through raw subprocess.run outside repo_inspection), INV-kuroj (XDG_STATE/XDG_CONFIG/~/hypergumbo writes bypass safety_zones; the offer runs from main(), outside every taint source), WI-puban (OpenRouter call, domain not in ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md). Cross-check: the opaque_boundary launch list is primitive names only ({subprocess.run, subprocess.Popen, Popen.communicate}) and matches the gate's process primitives exactly, but it does not name programs, so it cannot see the backend launches. EVIDENCE: on dev @ 0e6e72265c, scripts/check-io-allowlist -> 'OK — 264 site(s) in 224 reviewed entr(y/ies).' rc=0. Behavioural demo: appended def _demo_unlisted(): import subprocess as sp; sp.run(['curl', ...]) to hypergumbo_core/repo_fingerprint.py -> rc=1, 'NEW — 1 unlisted site key(s) ... hypergumbo_core.repo_fingerprint: function: _demo_unlisted primitive: subprocess.run family: process count: 1 (line 311)' (reverted). The same shape is pinned by tests/test_check_io_allowlist.py::test_live_tree_positive_control."  # c82b
